27:04.760 --> 27:08.821
item 1B. This is Marcus on a land disposal process overview.

27:09.562 --> 27:12.525
I think this has to do with the state— the new change,

27:12.542 --> 27:15.878
right? Yes, there have been changes in

27:16.378 --> 27:19.832
state law to how we conduct land disposals, and so we wanted to

27:19.881 --> 27:23.374
bring the issue for discussion. Also,

27:26.356 --> 27:30.082
we want to make sure we are on the right path as far as determining

27:30.262 --> 27:33.270
what is going to be insignificant versus significant land parcels.

27:33.867 --> 27:37.656
So under state law, cities have a lot of leeway

27:38.156 --> 27:41.678
in determining what are significant parcels of land and

27:41.775 --> 27:45.302
how you dispose of those. Significant parcels versus insignificant parcels

27:45.399 --> 27:48.560
is very different. But there's been

27:49.060 --> 27:51.813
a recent change in law that somewhat restricts that,

27:53.150 --> 27:56.838
and also that affects our timing of having public hearings.

27:58.007 --> 28:02.886
Traditionally, when conducting a land disposal,

28:03.239 --> 28:07.203
we would notice a public hearing prior to the authorization of the land disposal.

28:08.679 --> 28:11.905
If it's authorized, then we would do a contract and then bring it back for

28:12.405 --> 28:14.280
approval on the contract, and that would be done at a public meeting.

28:15.580 --> 28:19.383
Recent changes in state law basically reverse that. So now you would

28:19.883 --> 28:23.187
have a public meeting in which you authorize the land disposal, and then the contract

28:23.687 --> 28:26.334
would come back at a and be approved after a public hearing.

28:28.346 --> 28:32.315
And so we're—

28:32.957 --> 28:36.428
so currently our city ordinance requires a public hearing before authorizing the

28:36.557 --> 28:40.410
land disposal, and the state code requires public hearing before approving

28:40.910 --> 28:44.346
the contract. The request would be to just have

28:44.443 --> 28:47.794
one public hearing when we approve the contract, which is going to be required under

28:48.294 --> 28:51.850
state law, and if the council would be okay with altering the ordinance

28:52.350 --> 28:54.146
so that we don't have duplicative public hearings.

28:59.302 --> 29:02.508
Is there anybody who doesn't think that's a good idea? No, I just think it

29:02.524 --> 29:06.070
makes sense because there's expense involved when we're noticing things and different

29:06.570 --> 29:10.610
things like that. So as long as we're making it an open process and it's

29:11.110 --> 29:14.227
cleaned up, I think we should move forward with cleaning it up. Okay.

29:15.046 --> 29:18.775
And so in relation to That seems pretty straightforward, so we'll proceed

29:18.872 --> 29:22.092
with doing some code changes and bringing that before you.

