in a geothermal facility at this time in Eagle

04:47:07.708 --> 04:47:11.538
Mountain. I think we have time to go ahead and provide that opportunity

04:47:12.038 --> 04:47:15.295
for education to see if there's any additional changes to the requirements we need to

04:47:15.795 --> 04:47:18.528
make there. So So whether we, you know,

04:47:18.673 --> 04:47:22.137
pull that out at this time and address that later or we

04:47:22.637 --> 04:47:25.881
just leave it in and then refine it later, I think we have plenty of

04:47:25.914 --> 04:47:29.955
time to address that. When it comes to things like

04:47:30.504 --> 04:47:33.766
hazardous materials and storage and things like that, I think a lot

04:47:34.266 --> 04:47:39.002
of that will also be addressed more on a case-by-case basis because the

04:47:39.083 --> 04:47:42.739
types of materials, the quantity of materials, and all that sort of stuff

04:47:43.239 --> 04:47:46.798
That's not something we could ever really totally anticipate in

04:47:46.846 --> 04:47:50.539
a broad ordinance. That is going to be kind of a case-by-case basis. I'm not

04:47:51.039 --> 04:47:55.164
sure exactly how we would draft that right now to try and be all-encompassing.

04:47:56.561 --> 04:48:00.992
And in a similar light, with trying to name specific SMR technologies,

04:48:01.121 --> 04:48:04.525
I understand the desire with that because getting as specific

04:48:05.025 --> 04:48:07.993
as possible to the ones that we know, the ones that we trust, makes a

04:48:08.025 --> 04:48:11.353
lot of sense. In my research and

04:48:11.468 --> 04:48:15.280
in my work with different companies, the technologies

04:48:15.313 --> 04:48:19.252
are still evolving so rapidly. The cooling technologies,

04:48:19.350 --> 04:48:22.456
the fuel types, the designs,

04:48:23.845 --> 04:48:27.688
the size of the reactors— there's so many different variables right now that I

04:48:28.124 --> 04:48:31.840
worry that we could be inadvertently missing

04:48:32.020 --> 04:48:34.743
really good technologies. excluding those.

04:48:35.899 --> 04:48:39.014
And so my approach was to try and remove the ones

04:48:39.514 --> 04:48:42.531
that we know that are not going to be conducive to Eagle Mountain,

04:48:42.627 --> 04:48:45.533
the ones that are the high water users, the ones that carry more risk and

04:48:46.033 --> 04:48:49.226
things like that, and leave it open for now. But at the very least,

04:48:49.612 --> 04:48:52.887
as has been mentioned, you know, during the rezone application,

04:48:52.919 --> 04:48:56.195
during the development agreement, all these things come to light as far as what

04:48:56.695 --> 04:48:59.262
the technology is. We have to get to know the technology really good at that

04:48:59.762 --> 04:49:02.995
that point, and we can deny those at that point. If, if that new technology

04:49:03.027 --> 04:49:06.392
comes in, turns out to be something that is, you know, not,

04:49:06.472 --> 04:49:10.430
not ideal, then there's, there's no reason why we need to approve that.

04:49:11.423 --> 04:49:14.756
Um, I think there's, there's certainly some things that we can,

04:49:15.429 --> 04:49:19.194
um, you know, make changes as far as process

04:49:19.694 --> 04:49:22.895
goes. Um, you know, when it comes to,

04:49:24.001 --> 04:49:27.674
you know, site plan approvals and things like that, that's something that I I would

04:49:27.690 --> 04:49:31.352
feel comfortable making pretty obviously quick changes

04:49:31.852 --> 04:49:33.756
to that. I think that might even be something that could be changed at the

04:49:33.821 --> 04:49:38.190
dais right now if that's something that could be worded

04:49:38.690 --> 04:49:43.049
quickly. But if not, then we can bring back an amendment quite quickly for

04:49:43.162 --> 04:49:46.694
that. As far as research on distances for

04:49:47.308 --> 04:49:51.477
natural gas and geothermal as well, I think that one is

04:49:51.655 --> 04:49:55.963
obviously very well understood. Understood too that we want to be very considerate

04:49:56.027 --> 04:49:59.399
of that. I think a lot of that will actually be resolved or worked

04:49:59.899 --> 04:50:03.365
out before it actually gets to us when

04:50:03.865 --> 04:50:06.239
