04:50:21.752 --> 04:50:25.443
those have or what have you, again, we have our development agreements,

04:50:26.053 --> 04:50:29.345
our zoning requirements. We don't have to zone an area

04:50:29.845 --> 04:50:33.840
we don't feel comfortable with. If just natural gas in general, you don't

04:50:33.857 --> 04:50:37.100
want that anywhere near, let's say,

04:50:37.533 --> 04:50:41.066
you know, a mile from residential, it's up to you as

04:50:41.082 --> 04:50:44.663
a body who determines where that zoning goes to to just do that,

04:50:44.920 --> 04:50:48.356
right? That's— that you can create that policy for yourselves.

04:50:49.014 --> 04:50:52.338
So I think you have a lot of power already to start limiting that with

04:50:52.838 --> 04:50:56.159
or without the information you have now. Obviously, we'd still want to provide

04:50:56.659 --> 04:51:00.077
you plenty of information, education, so that you can make an educated decision.

04:51:00.254 --> 04:51:04.300
But I think you do have within what's here today a

04:51:04.348 --> 04:51:08.186
lot of capability to help steer what needs to happen to keep everyone safe

04:51:08.282 --> 04:51:10.041
and make sure the city is in a good spot.

04:51:16.310 --> 04:51:19.724
