06:26:39.954 --> 06:26:43.343
a bunch of more hoops to have a budget amendment and to allocate resources

06:26:43.843 --> 06:26:47.328
towards this, it's going to slow the process down. That's what I'm hearing and seeing.

06:26:47.506 --> 06:26:51.411
And so, I mean, originally I might have had some

06:26:51.540 --> 06:26:54.982
consternation about saying, OK, let's take some of what we've already budgeted.

06:26:55.209 --> 06:26:59.557
But as long as we have a pathway forward to replenish that come September,

06:26:59.638 --> 06:27:03.152
August, and it accelerates the timeline under which we can be building these,

06:27:03.281 --> 06:27:05.479
I'm going to be fine with that. I don't know how everyone else is going

06:27:05.512 --> 06:27:09.572
to feel about it. I just

06:27:09.588 --> 06:27:13.696
feel like we need to— we, we know we have problem

06:27:14.196 --> 06:27:18.479
areas in Silver Lake, and I would love to see some advancement of

06:27:18.655 --> 06:27:22.700
a speed table. I don't know how that's going to change the,

06:27:23.967 --> 06:27:27.175
the, the speed study will really change that reality

06:27:27.675 --> 06:27:30.990
that we already are already aware of. I'm not opposed to doing a speed

06:27:31.006 --> 06:27:34.581
study. I just think it'd be nice to— well, the thing is you don't

06:27:34.789 --> 06:27:37.915
want to put the improvements in without the data.

06:27:38.156 --> 06:27:41.362
Otherwise you open up the floodgates of putting them in wherever. So once you have

06:27:41.862 --> 06:27:44.856
the data and it justifies putting in the speed table, then you're on solid ground

06:27:44.888 --> 06:27:46.139
to move forward and the whole bit.

06:27:47.133 --> 06:27:50.643
Okay. I'm going to speak up here because I feel like we've,

06:27:50.739 --> 06:27:53.201
we've been very clear All 5 of us,

06:27:54.285 --> 06:27:57.847
and we're being frog walked on this. I mean, the reality of

06:27:58.347 --> 06:28:01.536
it is we've told you where we want them in the school zones. We set

06:28:01.585 --> 06:28:04.974
money aside from the utility sales so we don't have to jump through

06:28:05.474 --> 06:28:06.685
the hoops. That money is available now.

06:28:08.525 --> 06:28:11.009
I don't understand what the problem is here. I understand you don't want to do

06:28:11.025 --> 06:28:14.429
them. That's clear. I think it's been made clear by engineering.

06:28:14.510 --> 06:28:17.704
It's been made clear by our streets department. But the reality of it

06:28:18.204 --> 06:28:21.477
is. There's a problem there that will only be solved by cars having to

06:28:21.977 --> 06:28:24.955
stop. We've already had crossing guards be hit.

06:28:25.788 --> 06:28:28.596
Marie is one of them who isn't a crossing guard anymore, but she was hit

06:28:28.709 --> 06:28:32.261
right there because a car decided not to stop. So when

06:28:32.761 --> 06:28:34.979
do we wait? Do we wait until a kid's hit and killed and then,

06:28:35.100 --> 06:28:38.499
then it becomes a priority? One of

06:28:38.532 --> 06:28:42.462
my big concerns is that I

06:28:42.510 --> 06:28:45.888
feel like we're doing a Band-Aid on something

06:28:46.362 --> 06:28:49.443
that needs to be addressed with a bigger solution.

06:28:49.796 --> 06:28:52.909
I feel like especially down by the Silver Lake Elementary,

06:28:53.407 --> 06:28:56.922
we should be looking at a tunnel and we should use utility sale

06:28:56.954 --> 06:29:00.805
funds and just bite the bullet and do it because I

06:29:01.305 --> 06:29:04.785
don't think any amount of speed tables is going to solve the problem of

06:29:04.818 --> 06:29:08.814
people who don't want to follow the laws and

06:29:09.314 --> 06:29:12.392
keep kids safe, but a tunnel would make it better. And I,

06:29:13.207 --> 06:29:16.767
I, I want us to do what's right, but I'm also okay

06:29:16.783 --> 06:29:20.958
with spending the money we need to spend to give it the best option

06:29:21.395 --> 06:29:24.813
for keeping kids safe. The question is, is we've

06:29:25.313 --> 06:29:28.767
already made a motion on this, we've already allocated funds for it, we've already given

06:29:29.267 --> 06:29:31.344
direction. Why is it not in process?

06:29:33.873 --> 06:29:37.126
I would argue that it is in process, and the appropriate way to do it

06:29:37.626 --> 06:29:40.913
is to do the study first so you don't open up yourselves to the liability

06:29:41.025 --> 06:29:44.391
of, I put something in that's not justified by the study that

06:29:44.891 --> 06:29:48.445
doesn't meet MUTCD standards, and you put the city at liability, greater liability

06:29:48.477 --> 06:29:51.922
than not putting it in just off the

06:29:52.422 --> 06:29:55.768
dais. You follow engineering standards and protocols to do it

06:29:56.268 --> 06:29:59.262
appropriately, and then you are protected from all the liability.

06:29:59.839 --> 06:30:03.060
I know that you— all of us have our interpretations

06:30:03.560 --> 06:30:05.728
of what should or should not be But I tell you what, I am not

06:30:05.792 --> 06:30:09.255
an engineer, and I don't care, and I'm

06:30:09.755 --> 06:30:12.766
not trying to persuade you that you should or should not do something. I am

06:30:12.862 --> 06:30:16.041
telling you that the proper process and the first step

06:30:16.251 --> 06:30:19.689
is to do it with a study so that you protect the interest of our

06:30:19.722 --> 06:30:21.836
taxpayers and the liability therein.

06:30:23.680 --> 06:30:27.382
So you're saying your statement is then if we put a speed table in that

06:30:27.480 --> 06:30:31.446
we're opening up liability to the citizens? If it's a non-justified one,

06:30:31.542 --> 06:30:34.593
yes. If it's totally justified, put it in. If you should

06:30:35.093 --> 06:30:37.917
have a tunnel, put that in. I don't— I'm not an engineer,

06:30:38.446 --> 06:30:41.947
but what should happen is that an engineer should put a study together to tell

06:30:41.979 --> 06:30:45.656
you what you should do, then you follow that engineer's standard, and then you

06:30:45.672 --> 06:30:49.204
are safe and protected. But if we do it from the dais,

06:30:49.285 --> 06:30:53.363
then we're not listening to engineers and we're not doing it appropriately. Well, I actually

06:30:53.379 --> 06:30:56.655
contacted an engineering firm and asked this question. Question, and what you just said is

06:30:56.687 --> 06:31:00.380
baloney. I'm just going to tell you that. And it was Horrocks that I called.

06:31:01.439 --> 06:31:04.089
I had a discussion about engineering speed tables.

06:31:04.876 --> 06:31:08.601
They're like, that takes like 15 minutes. We're not talking about rocket science

06:31:08.649 --> 06:31:12.422
here. So I'm finding this hard to swallow. But Marcus, he's made

06:31:12.438 --> 06:31:16.003
a— he's made a statement that we're going to be legally

06:31:16.099 --> 06:31:18.973
liable if we do that. I'd like to have you give us some information.

06:31:19.310 --> 06:31:21.847
I'm not putting you on the spot here. But I'd like you to be able

06:31:21.896 --> 06:31:25.027
to provide that to us. If we're going to make statements like that, it ought

06:31:25.527 --> 06:31:28.158
to be substantiated instead of just throwing that out on the dais.

06:31:29.025 --> 06:31:32.075
And then once this is done, I want to come back and talk about this

06:31:32.575 --> 06:31:35.945
because there comes a point when we've said it for a year, we've allocated

06:31:36.445 --> 06:31:39.012
money to it, all 5 of us voted on it, and it's still not done,

06:31:39.060 --> 06:31:42.833
and you're telling us that we now need to go through these additional hoops where

06:31:43.333 --> 06:31:47.197
we already know where the problems are, where the crosswalks already exist. that we're going

06:31:47.229 --> 06:31:50.747
to pretend like those aren't the places that the speed tables go. They already

06:31:50.764 --> 06:31:53.862
exist in other cities. I doubt that it's as big a liability as you say

06:31:54.362 --> 06:31:57.604
it is because they're in the exact same places for elementary schools that we're talking

06:31:57.621 --> 06:32:00.635
about. So I think we need to go down that route. If you're going to

06:32:01.135 --> 06:32:03.424
make that statement, it ought to be substantiated, and if not, you ought to be

06:32:03.924 --> 06:32:04.552
prepared to defend that.

06:32:07.784 --> 06:32:11.285
I want to weigh in again if I can, quite quickly. David,

06:32:11.478 --> 06:32:12.998
how long does it take to get How long would it take to get the

06:32:13.498 --> 06:32:17.126
study done again? Probably 2 to 4 weeks. So 2 to 4 weeks, we should

06:32:17.239 --> 06:32:20.109
be able to know where we could evaluate that.

06:32:24.350 --> 06:32:27.906
I understand, I understand Councilmember Wood's frustration with trying to get something

06:32:27.938 --> 06:32:31.333
done. We've, we have pressed this for a while and, and to no

06:32:31.833 --> 06:32:35.299
avail. I'm going to say it that way. But it feels to me like we're

06:32:35.799 --> 06:32:39.967
starting to move forward and make the progress that we want. And so I

06:32:40.790 --> 06:32:43.761
know this may not sit well with him, and that's okay.

06:32:44.553 --> 06:32:47.217
I mean, I'm okay with waiting 2 to 4 weeks to get the data and

06:32:47.313 --> 06:32:51.145
to then reevaluate it, because what I'm not okay is not doing

06:32:51.177 --> 06:32:53.962
anything and not moving forward. I think there's gonna be other areas in the city

06:32:53.978 --> 06:32:58.181
we're gonna identify issues that we're not even aware of or that we're not

06:32:58.681 --> 06:33:02.320
contemplating. I think we're gonna have to amend some of the monies that we're setting

06:33:02.336 --> 06:33:05.176
aside for some of those areas, because it's a real issue citywide.

06:33:06.739 --> 06:33:11.118
I agree with you, Councilmember Wood, those elementary schools need some mitigation.

06:33:12.670 --> 06:33:15.760
They're not specific to just Silver Lake, by the way. We've talked about this in

06:33:15.793 --> 06:33:18.574
other places. Mountain Trails has the same problem.

06:33:19.110 --> 06:33:22.536
Blackridge has the same problem. Completely agree. And, and so

06:33:22.617 --> 06:33:28.242
my, my, my point is simply that we need to do something, and we've

06:33:28.274 --> 06:33:32.165
kind of not been able to accomplish a lot in the last— I've been

06:33:32.665 --> 06:33:35.692
on the council coming up on 4 and a half years, and I've been trying

06:33:35.805 --> 06:33:39.453
to get something done here and been pretty unsuccessful at it.

06:33:39.501 --> 06:33:41.509
What I find is, as a single council member, you can't get a whole lot

06:33:41.525 --> 06:33:44.963
done at all, but as a group of council members, you can accomplish a lot.

06:33:45.060 --> 06:33:48.579
And I think that we've moved this ball forward. I think staff recognizes and understands

06:33:49.079 --> 06:33:51.765
that this is a priority that we're going to accomplish this year,

06:33:53.567 --> 06:33:57.058
and so I'm willing to give them some leeway and to trust the

06:33:57.558 --> 06:34:00.960
data. I mean, I've had to say that in other circumstances

06:34:01.297 --> 06:34:04.219
and just look at it and then to really evaluate.

06:34:04.348 --> 06:34:07.511
I don't know if a speed hump, a speed bump,

06:34:07.896 --> 06:34:11.236
a swell— I mean, I have my doubts about

06:34:11.252 --> 06:34:14.640
whether some traffic calming paint on the side of the road

06:34:15.140 --> 06:34:17.450
is going to make much of an impact, but I think there needs to be

06:34:17.950 --> 06:34:21.735
something that impedes traffic flow and slows it down. Speed table

06:34:22.235 --> 06:34:25.485
makes sense because we have crosswalks and safety issues for those kids.

06:34:25.549 --> 06:34:28.594
To me, that makes a lot of sense. But again, I'm not a traffic engineer.

06:34:29.059 --> 06:34:32.488
I don't have that expertise, and David and his team do. And so

06:34:32.504 --> 06:34:35.805
I'm going to ask him to evaluate that with the traffic engineers and come to

06:34:36.305 --> 06:34:39.154
us and tell us where it needs to be that way. So I just want

06:34:39.654 --> 06:34:42.023
to be clear, I'm supportive of a study,

06:34:43.257 --> 06:34:46.189
but I'm also— once we have that study,

06:34:46.526 --> 06:34:50.219
like the next day. I would love to see some action being taken in Silver

06:34:50.719 --> 06:34:53.575
Lake. And the mayor, we talked earlier, he talked, you know, we have so many

06:34:53.672 --> 06:34:56.931
priorities in the city that David Salazar is probably feeling

06:34:57.431 --> 06:34:59.950
like, I don't know which road to work on today, you know?

06:35:00.656 --> 06:35:04.124
And I'm just gonna say Silver Lake for me is an area that we need

06:35:04.624 --> 06:35:06.533
to address ASAP. That's like top of my list.

06:35:07.834 --> 06:35:10.949
So if we can get something done before school starts, that would be awesome.

06:35:11.270 --> 06:35:14.543
Thank you. I think given the speed with which the study

06:35:14.559 --> 06:35:17.728
can be done, it makes sense to not go through budgetary hoops. And it makes

06:35:18.228 --> 06:35:21.025
sense at this point to allocate some of the money for the speed tables over

06:35:21.525 --> 06:35:24.920
to the study because we can get it done fast. And as soon as that

06:35:25.420 --> 06:35:29.285
study comes back, then we— Yeah, yeah, it's already in there. And we

06:35:29.785 --> 06:35:32.210
have enough money to pay for the study, and we have enough money to— even

06:35:32.259 --> 06:35:35.264
once the study comes back, we have enough money to immediately start on some of

06:35:35.313 --> 06:35:38.404
the action items. So that's where I'm falling in line with

06:35:38.420 --> 06:35:42.059
what Councilmember Wright is saying as well. So do

06:35:42.559 --> 06:35:46.830
we need a motion to direct staff to move forward with the plan, or— well,

06:35:46.895 --> 06:35:49.811
it says possible action, so I'm just wondering,

06:35:51.853 --> 06:35:55.365
Marcus, do we have to do a motion for this, or— Typically when you're taking

06:35:55.381 --> 06:35:58.845
action to direct staff— Sassy. You could have just said yes.

06:35:59.612 --> 06:36:02.626
It's late. Yes. Yes, Councilmember Clark.

06:36:03.372 --> 06:36:06.576
Thank you, Council Member Clark. I appreciate it. I just want

06:36:07.076 --> 06:36:09.380
to— if you're going to make that type of a motion, I want to make

06:36:09.880 --> 06:36:13.209
sure that we're setting clear expectations and priorities. Other projects will

06:36:13.709 --> 06:36:15.501
be put on hold, uh, I assume.

06:36:16.494 --> 06:36:19.875
And the expectation that if this takes 2

06:36:20.375 --> 06:36:23.880
to 4 weeks, that's the, the possibly the—

06:36:23.944 --> 06:36:26.925
let's say it's the 6th of August, because I know that's a Thursday.

06:36:27.950 --> 06:36:31.459
We wouldn't meet as a council to approve whatever the study says.

06:36:32.052 --> 06:36:35.280
Until the second meeting in August. That's not

06:36:35.780 --> 06:36:38.571
even construction. That's the study to look at.

06:36:38.620 --> 06:36:41.686
So, so, so to say that there will be a speed table in there by

06:36:42.186 --> 06:36:46.006
the time school starts around the 15th of August is, is absolutely unrealistic,

06:36:46.022 --> 06:36:49.442
correct? That's correct. And 2 to 4 weeks is an ideal situation.

06:36:49.554 --> 06:36:52.814
We're— I mean, we're assuming the consultant can start right away. I do have

06:36:52.910 --> 06:36:56.282
2 who can, but I still haven't gone out to bid for a short bid

06:36:56.782 --> 06:36:59.880
time because we're going to be under the $75,000 threshold, which will be helpful.

06:36:59.928 --> 06:37:03.349
So it will go quickly. To get it done before school is going to

06:37:03.849 --> 06:37:07.236
be a stretch. We did paint Silver Lake. That's something we're looking at.

06:37:07.702 --> 06:37:11.252
Zach and I have talked about another immediate solution to address

06:37:11.943 --> 06:37:15.332
the speeding there. We've talked about Brookhaven, and we're looking at some things to do

06:37:15.832 --> 06:37:19.508
there as well. So we, we hear your concerns, and just

06:37:20.008 --> 06:37:24.841
from an engineering standpoint, I'm, I'm not against any of these solutions. I'm just

06:37:25.341 --> 06:37:28.403
looking for the best solution for all these locations. What if while we're getting the

06:37:28.483 --> 06:37:31.918
answers back and we're getting the ball moving,

06:37:32.351 --> 06:37:36.572
we ask that, uh, Chief Knutson has

06:37:36.684 --> 06:37:40.167
some of his deputies really take a special interest in

06:37:40.215 --> 06:37:43.425
that area until we can get whatever measure we're

06:37:43.925 --> 06:37:47.406
putting into place? Because we all know that it's an issue there specifically,

06:37:47.919 --> 06:37:51.322
and I think If we can't get something done by the time school starts,

06:37:51.450 --> 06:37:54.516
let's use the deputies that we have to help us with that.

06:37:55.222 --> 06:37:58.993
Are you talking specifically during the crossing of the school kids, or are you talking

06:37:59.493 --> 06:38:01.930
just in general? I think during the crossing,

06:38:02.219 --> 06:38:05.493
because that's when the problem mostly is. So we're

06:38:05.993 --> 06:38:09.907
talking later in August, spot checks during the

06:38:10.051 --> 06:38:13.197
crossing hours before and after school? Yeah, and I would drop the hammer on the

06:38:13.697 --> 06:38:16.680
people who are driving through there in such a hurry so that they're all like,

06:38:17.376 --> 06:38:20.954
we're not going to do this anymore for at least 2 weeks so

06:38:21.454 --> 06:38:23.674
that they know they're going to get ticketed if they're not doing what they're supposed

06:38:27.326 --> 06:38:30.706
All year long. Well, the thing is, is down

06:38:30.738 --> 06:38:33.536
in Saratoga at Foothill and whatever road Lakeview's on,

06:38:34.215 --> 06:38:37.618
that's a horrible intersection right there. It's super scary. The dude

06:38:38.118 --> 06:38:41.903
who crosses there wears a like a body cam,

06:38:42.176 --> 06:38:45.639
and they forever, when they first started that intersection with

06:38:45.687 --> 06:38:48.910
the light, they had cop cars there to pull

06:38:49.410 --> 06:38:52.374
people over, and they did, and I think that really improved that intersection.

06:38:52.775 --> 06:38:56.430
So if we can get some attention there to get some improvement

06:38:56.930 --> 06:38:59.782
until we can get whatever we're building built, I think that's a good,

06:39:00.295 --> 06:39:03.983
like— Intro. Yeah, thank you. But to

06:39:04.483 --> 06:39:06.773
say, but so I just wanted to be clear, to say this will be done

06:39:07.273 --> 06:39:11.197
before school is unrealistic. So I want to make sure that— That's

06:39:11.697 --> 06:39:15.203
why I made the point about simultaneously, like, let's do the study, but let's put

06:39:15.703 --> 06:39:18.969
in a speed table. I don't know what other alternatives, like a

06:39:19.469 --> 06:39:23.039
tunnel is— Expensive. It's like

06:39:23.539 --> 06:39:27.478
$1 million or more. And is— Well, there's bulb-outs.

06:39:27.526 --> 06:39:31.148
There's other things we can do too. The speed tables are great where they

06:39:31.212 --> 06:39:34.468
work, but we have concerns about diversion traffic. need to look at that as well.

06:39:35.239 --> 06:39:38.453
There's already speeding on Silver Creek Way.

06:39:38.935 --> 06:39:42.182
If we put a speed table there, that could also start to have more

06:39:42.230 --> 06:39:45.908
traffic heading north cutting through Golden Meadow Road as

06:39:46.022 --> 06:39:48.860
well. So that's something we have to look at in the study. When you put

06:39:49.360 --> 06:39:51.926
a table, people also are going to be slamming on their brakes more, they accelerate.

06:39:51.974 --> 06:39:55.137
There's other factors we have to look at as well. Like, it's not just like

06:39:55.637 --> 06:39:58.187
a one and done. So we want to look at all the options and present

06:39:58.687 --> 06:39:59.058
the best one for you guys.

06:40:04.160 --> 06:40:08.872
I make a motion.

06:40:09.453 --> 06:40:14.673
All right, Mayor, I move that the City Council proceed with the speed

06:40:14.689 --> 06:40:18.520
studies outlined in 18A, adding the roads identified

06:40:18.568 --> 06:40:22.215
by Councilmember Wood. I don't think there were any other Woods, right?

06:40:22.297 --> 06:40:23.689
There were only 2, the ones you added.

06:40:26.765 --> 06:40:30.416
And funding this from money previously allocated to

06:40:30.916 --> 06:40:35.222
speed tables. And I think

06:40:35.722 --> 06:40:39.681
that's it. Second. I do too. All right.

06:40:39.777 --> 06:40:42.839
So we have a motion by Councilmember Whiting and a second by Councilmember

06:40:43.339 --> 06:40:45.643
Wright. And any questions?

06:40:47.580 --> 06:40:50.763
Councilmember Wright? Yes. Councilmember Whiting? Yes.

06:40:50.844 --> 06:40:54.372
Councilmember Wood? No. Councillor Heriot?

06:40:56.635 --> 06:40:58.427
Yes, but I still want a speed table.

06:41:00.259 --> 06:41:01.586
Councillor Clerk? Yes.

06:41:08.784 --> 06:41:11.509
Okay.

06:41:12.542 --> 06:41:16.429
All right. I think we have clear direction

06:41:16.929 --> 06:41:20.228
there. Last thing is any legislative

06:41:20.728 --> 06:41:24.311
items from John Magnus. John's coming out for midnight with

06:41:24.811 --> 06:41:29.072
us. Give him a minute. I— Turn it

06:41:29.572 --> 06:41:32.428
on. It's on. You're on. Oh, it is on.

06:41:34.077 --> 06:41:37.943
Okay. Um, 2 items tonight. So I looked into the Bitcoin,

06:41:38.202 --> 06:41:41.842
uh, using as payment. Our vendor that processes our payments— I

06:41:42.342 --> 06:41:45.816
heard Bitcoin. I'm listening. Our vendor who processes

06:41:45.864 --> 06:41:50.812
our payments does not take PayPal

06:41:50.989 --> 06:41:54.201
or the other Bitcoin purse that you can use to pay your bills.

06:41:54.736 --> 06:42:00.441
So right now, it's not an option for us to use cryptocurrency

